    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0569" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 119.28/a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé O’Shaughnessy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-12T10:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1914, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>742. We are just informed that message No. 741, April 11, 9 p.m., sent from here
                    has been stopped by censor and delivery refused. Investigate at once and demand
                    message.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
